{
    "background_story": "Mohammad was a 19th-century Persian poet known for his mastery of classical forms. Among his favorite forms was the tetrameter, a meter consisting of four beats per line. He spent years perfecting his craft, pouring his heart and soul into his verses. Mohammad's poetry was renowned for its musical quality, with each line flowing smoothly into the next. His tetrameter verses, in particular, were celebrated for their ability to evoke powerful emotions and paint vivid pictures. One of his most famous poems, 'The Nightingale's Lament', was written in tetrameter and told the story of a bird's longing for its lost love. The poem's beauty and melancholy captivated readers, cementing Mohammad's reputation as one of the greatest poets of his time.",
